INFO 02-21 09:28:47 logger.py:39] Received request cmpl-83f64106c4544ad9ad23a8c982aaf8f0-0: prompt: 'Here is some R code that you can use to summarize the patient table and create pie and bar charts:\n```\n# Load the patient table into a dataframe\npatient_data <- read.csv("patient_table.csv", header = TRUE)\n\n# Summarize the number of patients by diabetes type\ndiabetes_type_counts <- table(patient_data$Diabetes.Type)\n\n# Create a pie chart to visualize the diabetes type counts\npie(diabetes_type_counts, labels = names(diabetes_type_counts), main = "Diabetes Type Counts")\n\n# Summarize the number of patients by treatment\ntreatment_counts <- table(patient_data$Treatment)\n\n# Create a bar chart to visualize the treatment counts\nbarplot(treatment_counts, xlab = "Treatment", ylab = "Count", main = "Treatment Counts")\n```\nThis code will first load the patient table into a dataframe, then it will use the `table()` function to summarize the number of patients by diabetes type and treatment. The resulting counts are then used to create a pie chart for the diabetes type counts and a bar chart for the treatment counts.\n\nYou can customize the charts by adding colors, labels and title using the appropriate chart function, for example in the pie chart you can use `col` to change the color of the sections.\n\nYou can also use ggplot2 package to create more visually appealing charts.\n```\nlibrary(ggplot2)\nggplot(patient_data, aes(x = Diabetes.Type)) + geom_bar(aes(y = (..count..)/sum(..count..)))+\n  ggtitle("Diabetes Type Counts") +\n  xlab("Diabetes Type") +\n  ylab("Percentage of patients") +\n  scale_y_continuous(labels = scales::percent)\n```\nIt will show the same information but with a more polished look.\n\nPlease note that this code assumes that your patient table is in a CSV file called "patient\\_table.csv" and that the column names in the table match the ones used in the code. You may need to adjust the code accordingly if your table has different column names or if it is in a different format.', params: SamplingParams(n=1, presence_penalty=0.0, frequency_penalty=0.0, repetition_penalty=1.0, temperature=0.0, top_p=1.0, top_k=-1, min_p=0.0, seed=None, stop=[], stop_token_ids=[], bad_words=[], include_stop_str_in_output=False, ignore_eos=False, max_tokens=14, min_tokens=0, logprobs=None, prompt_logprobs=None, skip_special_tokens=True, spaces_between_special_tokens=True, truncate_prompt_tokens=None, guided_decoding=None), prompt_token_ids: [128000, 8586, 374, 1063, 432, 2082, 430, 499, 649, 1005, 311, 63179, 279, 8893, 2007, 323, 1893, 4447, 323, 3703, 27223, 512, 14196, 4077, 2, 9069, 279, 8893, 2007, 1139, 264, 39328, 198, 23557, 1807, 9297, 1373, 11468, 446, 23557, 5350, 11468, 498, 4342, 284, 8378, 696, 2, 8279, 5730, 553, 279, 1396, 315, 6978, 555, 20335, 955, 198, 8747, 16629, 1857, 27067, 9297, 2007, 79937, 1807, 3, 22427, 16629, 10394, 696, 2, 4324, 264, 4447, 9676, 311, 51187, 279, 20335, 955, 14921, 198, 20898, 56593, 16629, 1857, 27067, 11, 9382, 284, 5144, 56593, 16629, 1857, 27067, 705, 1925, 284, 330, 22427, 16629, 4078, 86759, 5240, 2, 8279, 5730, 553, 279, 1396, 315, 6978, 555, 6514, 198, 83, 35320, 27067, 9297, 2007, 79937, 1807, 3, 99654, 696, 2, 4324, 264, 3703, 9676, 311, 51187, 279, 6514, 14921, 198, 2308, 4569, 1175, 35320, 27067, 11, 865, 14717, 284, 330, 99654, 498, 379, 14717, 284, 330, 2568, 498, 1925, 284, 330, 99654, 86759, 1158, 14196, 4077, 2028, 2082, 690, 1176, 2865, 279, 8893, 2007, 1139, 264, 39328, 11, 1243, 433, 690, 1005, 279, 1595, 2048, 55358, 734, 311, 63179, 279, 1396, 315, 6978, 555, 20335, 955, 323, 6514, 13, 578, 13239, 14921, 527, 1243, 1511, 311, 1893, 264, 4447, 9676, 369, 279, 20335, 955, 14921, 323, 264, 3703, 9676, 369, 279, 6514, 14921, 382, 2675, 649, 32187, 279, 27223, 555, 7999, 8146, 11, 9382, 323, 2316, 1701, 279, 8475, 9676, 734, 11, 369, 3187, 304, 279, 4447, 9676, 499, 649, 1005, 1595, 2119, 63, 311, 2349, 279, 1933, 315, 279, 14491, 382, 2675, 649, 1101, 1005, 