{'model': '/data/model/deepseek-aiDeepSeek-R1-Distill-Qwen-7B', 'prompt': 'Certainly, there are other common disputes related to distribution agreements, including:\n\n1. Delayed delivery of goods: The distributor may claim that the manufacturer or supplier failed to deliver goods on time, impacting business operations or causing financial losses.\nEvidence required: The contract specifying delivery terms, records of delivery dates and delays, correspondence related to delivery disputes, and documentation of any financial impact resulting from delayed deliveries.\n2. Transit damage: The distributor may claim that the goods were damaged during transportation and are now unsellable or require costly repairs.\nEvidence required: The contract specifying responsibility for transportation and handling, photographs or records of damaged goods, inspection reports, correspondence related to transit damage disputes, and documentation of any financial impact due to damaged goods.\n3. Quantity disputes: One party may claim that the goods delivered were in a lesser quantity than agreed upon in the contract.\nEvidence required: The contract specifying quantity terms, records of orders and deliveries, correspondence related to quantity disputes, and documentation of any financial impact due to the disputed quantities.\n4. Warranty and return disputes: The parties may disagree on warranty claims, return policies, or the handling of returned goods.\nEvidence required: The contract specifying warranty and return terms, records of warranty claims and returns, correspondence related to warranty and return disputes, and documentation of any financial impact due to warranty or return disagreements.\n5. Price disputes: The parties may disagree on the pricing of goods or changes to pricing over time.\nEvidence required: The contract specifying pricing terms, records of agreed-upon prices and any price changes, correspondence related to pricing disputes, and documentation of any financial impact due to pricing disagreements.\n6. Unfair competition: One party may claim that the other party engaged in unfair competition, such as price undercutting or predatory practices.\nEvidence required: The contract specifying any competition-related terms, proof of the alleged unfair competition practices, correspondence related to competition disputes, and documentation of any financial impact due to the alleged unfair competition.\n7. Regulatory compliance: One party may claim that the other party failed to comply with applicable laws and regulations, resulting in penalties or other negative consequences.\nEvidence required: The contract specifying compliance responsibilities, records of regulatory violations, correspondence related to compliance disputes, and documentation of any penalties or financial impact due to non-compliance.\n\nThis list is not exhaustive, as various other disputes can arise depending on the specific terms of the distribution agreement and the circumstances surrounding the business relationship. However, this expanded list should provide a better understanding of the common disputes that can occur in distribution agreements.', 'temperature': 0.0, 'best_of': 1, 'max_tokens': 1407, 'logprobs': None, 'stream': True, 'stream_options': {'include_usage': True}}
{'model': '/data/model/deepseek-aiDeepSeek-R1-Distill-Qwen-7B', 'prompt': "Sure, here's the updated code:\n```python\nimport pandas as pd\nimport numpy as np\nimport re\nimport nltk\nnltk.download('omw-1.4')\nnltk.download('wordnet')\nfrom nltk.corpus import stopwords\nfrom nltk.tokenize import word_tokenize\nfrom nltk.stem import WordNetLemmatizer\nfrom sklearn.feature_extraction.text import TfidfVectorizer\nfrom sklearn.model_selection import KFold\nfrom sklearn.utils.class_weight import compute_class_weight\nfrom sklearn.svm import SVC\nfrom sklearn.metrics import f1_score\nfrom auto_tqdm import tqdm\n\n# Set seed value\nnp.random.seed(42)\n\n# Load data\ntrain_df = pd.read_csv('train.csv')\ntest_df = pd.read_csv('test.csv')\n\n# Compute class weights\nclass_weights = compute_class_weight(class_weight='balanced', classes=np.unique(train_df['label']), y=train_df['label'])\n\n# Define text pre-processing functions\ndef preprocess_text(text):\n    # Remove non-alphabetic characters\n    text = re.sub(r'[^a-zA-Z\\s]', '', text)\n    # Convert to lowercase\n    text = text.lower()\n    # Tokenize\n    tokens = word_tokenize(text)\n    # Remove stopwords\n    tokens = [token for token in tokens if token not in stopwords.words('english')]\n    # Lemmatize\n    lemmatizer = WordNetLemmatizer()\n    tokens = [lemmatizer.lemmatize(token) for token in tokens]\n    # Join tokens back into a string\n    text = ' '.join(tokens)\n    return text\n\n# Preprocess train and test text data with progress bar\nwith tqdm(total=len(train_df), desc='Preprocessing train text', dynamic_ncols=True) as pbar:\n    train_df['text'] = train_df['text'].apply(lambda x: preprocess_text(x))\n    pbar.update(len(train_df))\n\nwith tqdm(total=len(test_df), desc='Preprocessing test text', dynamic_ncols=True) as pbar:\n    test_df['text'] = test_df['text'].apply(lambda x: preprocess_text(x))\n    pbar.update(len(test_df))\n\n# Define KFold cross-validation with progress bar\nkf = KFold(n_splits=5, shuffle=True, random_state=42)\ntotal_iterations = kf.get_n_splits(train_df) * 2  # 2 iterations per fold (train\n```", 'temperature': 0.0, 'best_of': 1, 'max_tokens': 1091, 'logprobs': None, 'stream': True, 'stream_options': {'include_usage': True}}
