{'model': '/data/model/deepseek-aiDeepSeek-R1-Distill-Qwen-7B', 'prompt': 'Sure, here\'s a new description for the video script we created for idea 1 "Why Eating More Can Actually Help You Lose Weight":\n\nAre you tired of feeling hungry all the time in your weight loss journey? What if we told you that you could eat more and still lose weight? That\'s right, folks! In this video, we\'re going to explore the surprising science behind how eating more can actually help you shed those extra pounds. We\'ll bust some common weight loss myths and provide tips for incorporating metabolism-boosting foods into your diet. Plus, stick around until the end for a bonus tip that can take your weight loss efforts to the next level. Don\'t miss out on this game-changing information - hit that play button now and join us for the ultimate guide to healthy weight loss!', 'temperature': 0.0, 'best_of': 1, 'max_tokens': 1417, 'logprobs': None, 'stream': True, 'stream_options': {'include_usage': True}}
{'model': '/data/model/deepseek-aiDeepSeek-R1-Distill-Qwen-7B', 'prompt': "Here's an updated version of your resume with some suggestions for improvement:\n\nHou Kaku\nTokyo, Japan | 080-3091-9521 | [hou.kaku@gmail.com](mailto:hou.kaku@gmail.com) | linkedin.com/in/hou-kaku-a414a9268\n\nPROFESSIONAL SUMMARY\n\n* Results-driven QA Assurance and Test Automation Manager with 10+ years of experience in software engineering, project management, and team leadership.\n* Demonstrated expertise in developing, implementing, and managing test strategies, plans, and frameworks that increase efficiency and quality.\n* Strong communication skills with experience working with domestic and overseas teams in the US, Europe, and China.\n* Proficient in logic thinking, algorithms, and programming languages including C, C++, Python, Java, SQL, HTML, Shell, and Perl.\n\nWORK EXPERIENCE\nQuality Assurance Manager (Ichiba Backoffice, Logistics) - Rakuten Group, Inc. - Tokyo, Japan\nJanuary 2021 – Present\n\n* Lead and supervise a team of 15+ members across several departments and manage multiple projects and releases for 10+ Rakuten Ichiba Backoffice and Logistics-related products.\n* Develop and execute test strategies, plans, and guidelines for different SDLC (Agile, iterative, and waterfall) and collaborate with test automation to reduce test time by 35%.\n* Manage 3+ manual and automation QA teams and collaborate with 3+ vendor companies to reduce costs by 20%.\n* Create and propose budgets and estimations for 3 years and implement a continuous improvement culture.\n* Develop onboarding and training processes to grow a team of 10+ employees and subcontractors.\n\nTest Automation Manager (Ichiba Backoffice, Logistics) - Rakuten Group, Inc. - Tokyo, Japan\nMay 2018 – December 2020\n\n* Design and propose automation strategies for 10+ products and develop a hybrid automation framework using Cucumber and Selenium that decreases test execution time by 90%.\n* Design and implement 1000+ scenarios and functions test cases, detect 5+ bugs for each execution, cover 60% of manual test cases, and reduce 50% cost and 90% time of registration time.\n* Create a CI/CD system using Jenkins that runs test cases at midnight and reports bugs in the next morning.\n* Automate OMGR batch server using SSH commands and create orders using basket API that boost productivity by 900%.\n\nQuality Assurance Lead (Android system) - Sony Mobile Communications Inc. - Tokyo, Japan\nNovember 2012 - April 2017\n\n* Develop system test plans and design test cases for Android smartphones from Jellybean to Oreo 5+ versions and 10+ devices.\n* Implement automation test suites and integrate them into the CI/CD process using Jenkins to ensure daily tests can be executed for each release version.\n* Lead a 10+ QA team, detect 100 bugs out of 200 overall by analyzing the weak areas of the system.\n\nSenior Software Engineer (Symbian S60) - Sony Mobile Communications Inc. - Tokyo, Japan\nJune 2011 - October 2012\n\n* Develop Symbian S60 FOTA system in 3 months only to meet the release target.\n* Identify and fix bugs of Symbian S60 Device Management system by inserting logs, reducing 50% of the cost and time of bug fixing.\n\nSoftware Engineer (Symbian V9) - Fujitsu Broad Solution & Consulting Inc. - Tokyo, Japan\nAugust 2008 – May 2010\n\n* Design and implement T9 and ATOK based text input systems for Symbian V9 mobile phones with a 10-person team using C++ and achieve software quality targets with a bug ratio of less than 1%.\n\nJunior Software Engineer", 'temperature': 0.0, 'best_of': 1, 'max_tokens': 1032, 'logprobs': None, 'stream': True, 'stream_options': {'include_usage': True}}
{'model': '/data/model/deepseek-aiDeepSeek-R1-Distill-Qwen-7B', 'prompt': 'RESUME\n\nName: [Your Name]\nEmail: [Your Email]\nPhone: [Your Phone Number]\nLocation: [Your Location]\n\nPROFESSIONAL SUMMARY\nExperienced Quality Assurance Manager and Software Engineer with over 10 years of experience in software development and QA assurance. Skilled in leadership, logic thinking, and communication. Able to manage teams and projects, as well as develop and implement multiple test cases and plans. Excels at negotiating with domestic and overseas teams in the US, Europe, and China. Seeking a challenging role that will leverage my expertise in automation and testing.\n\nEXPERIENCE\n\nQuality Assurance Manager (Ichiba Backoffice, Logistics)\nRakuten Group, Inc., Tokyo, Japan\nJanuary 2021 – Present\n\n* Supervised a quality assurance team of 15+ members across several departments, completed more than 100 projects and release for 10+ Rakuten Ichiba Backoffice and Logistics related products.\n* Managed and led 3+ manual and automation QA teams across different projects, managing QA tasks in different SDLC (Agile, iterative and waterfall).\n* Collaborated with Test Automation to plan efforts for releases and decreased test time by 35%.\n* Created test strategy and test plan including each test level and type that suitable for different SDLC.\n* Dealt with 3+ vendor company and created test productivity guideline to reduce 20% cost.\n* Created software lifecycle test plan that support for 10 products and identified requirement leakage and shortage.\n* Created and proposed budget and estimation for 3 years and made a continues improvement culture.\n* Developed onboarding and training process regarding quality assurance practices and procedures and grew 10+ employees and subcontractor with growth, build up team and power up team efficiently.\n\nTest Automation Manager (Ichiba Backoffice, Logistics)\nRakuten Group, Inc., Tokyo, Japan\nMay 2018 – December 2020\n\n* Created automation strategy and proposed with department for 10+ products.\n* The first one in Rakuten that created and designed test framework that using API to create test data.\n* The first one in Rakuten that automated OMGR batch server using SSH command that boost up 900%\n* The first one in Rakuten that automatized create orders using basket API that boost up 900% productivity.\n* Designed a CI/CD system using Jenkins that run test cases in midnight and report bugs in the next morning.\n* Oversaw the test team’s creation of a Hybrid Automation Framework using Cucumber and Selenium that resulted in a decrease in test execution time to 90%.\n* Design and implemented 1000+ scenarios and functions test cases, detected 5+ bugs for each execution, covered 60% of manual test cases, reduced 50% cost and 90% time of registration time.\n\nQuality Assurance Lead (Android system)\nSony Mobile Communications Inc., Tokyo, Japan\nNovember 2012 - April 2017\n\n* Accessed and escalated the risk of system and bugs that could delay development and QA, in hence could make sure 10+ projects completed on schedule.\n* Made system test plan and designed test cases for Android smartphone from Jellybean to Oreo 5+ versions and 10+ devices.\n* Implemented automation test suite and integrated to CI/CD process using Jenkins that could make sure daily test could be executed for each release version.\n* Led a 10+ QA team, detected 100 bugs of 200 overall by analyzing the weak area of system.\n\nSenior Software Engineer (Symbian S60)\nSony Mobile Communications Inc., Tokyo, Japan\nJune 2011 - October 2012\n\n* Developed on Symbian S60 FOTA system in 3 months only to meet the release target.\n* Identified and fixed bugs of Symbian S60 Device Management', 'temperature': 0.0, 'best_of': 1, 'max_tokens': 1030, 'logprobs': None, 'stream': True, 'stream_options': {'include_usage': True}}
