{'model': '/data/model/deepseek-aiDeepSeek-R1-Distill-Qwen-7B', 'prompt': "In the Safeway, Ruby is hired by Katrina despite her lack of experience in cleaning. She is tasked with cleaning the bathrooms but is uncomfortable with the task. Meanwhile, Min is in the deli section and meets Mina, who is a deli worker like him. They bond over their shared love for Boar's Head products and Min finds a brochure for the products. When he looks at the back of the brochure, he sees a picture of his mother holding a Boar's Head product and realizes she works there.", 'temperature': 0.0, 'best_of': 1, 'max_tokens': 1087, 'logprobs': None, 'stream': True, 'stream_options': {'include_usage': True}}
{'model': '/data/model/deepseek-aiDeepSeek-R1-Distill-Qwen-7B', 'prompt': 'Based on the information provided in the first content, the following are potential headings for an article about Deed of Novation:\n\n1. What is a Deed of Novation?\n2. How is a Deed of Novation different from a Contract?\n3. Why Engage a Commercial Contract Lawyer to Review a Deed of Novation?\n4. The Purpose of a Deed of Novation\n5. Options when Deciding How to Address a Novation\n6. Risks Associated with a Deed of Novation\n7. How to Draft a Deed of Novation\n8. How a Deed of Novation Needs to be Signed\n\nThese headings could be adjusted or combined as necessary to create a well-structured and informative article.', 'temperature': 0.0, 'best_of': 1, 'max_tokens': 1050, 'logprobs': None, 'stream': True, 'stream_options': {'include_usage': True}}
{'model': '/data/model/deepseek-aiDeepSeek-R1-Distill-Qwen-7B', 'prompt': "I'm sorry, I am unable to create an table. I can organize the information in a bullet point format or a list format.\n\nTile:\n\n* The --tile parameter generates images that can be used as repeating tiles to create seamless patterns for fabrics, wallpapers, and textures.\n* --tile works with Model Versions 1, 2, 3.\n* --tile only generates a single tile.\n* Use a pattern making tool like this Seamless Pattern Checker to see the tile repeat.\n\nPrompt Examples:\n\n* prompt colorful tiger stripes --test --tile\n* example of the motif image and tiled repeat created with the midjourney tile parameter\n* prompt torn cardboard roses --testp --tile\n* example of the motif image and tiled repeat created with the midjourney tile parameter\n\nHow to Use the Tile Parameter:\n\n* Add --tile to the end of your prompt.\n* Animated Gif showing how the Midjourney tile parameter is typed.\n\nNote: Using a pattern making tool like Seamless Pattern Checker to see the tile repeat.", 'temperature': 0.0, 'best_of': 1, 'max_tokens': 1400, 'logprobs': None, 'stream': True, 'stream_options': {'include_usage': True}}
{'model': '/data/model/deepseek-aiDeepSeek-R1-Distill-Qwen-7B', 'prompt': "Based on the additional context provided, here's an overview of the data structures involved in the system:\n\n1. `doctor.workHours`: This is an array of objects representing the doctor's availability. Each object contains the start and end time in minutes since the beginning of the week (in UTC) and flags for queue and appointment availability.\n2. `doctor.nonWorkingDays`: This is an array of ordinal numbers representing the days of the week the doctor is unavailable. Sunday is represented by 0, Monday by 1, and so on.\n\nThe conversion from the database format to the front-end format involves:\n\n1. Converting the `workHours` array into an object with keys for each day of the week.\n2. Splitting any hour ranges that belong to two different days.\n3. Removing the hour ranges for days marked as unavailable in `nonWorkingDays`.\n\nNow that I have a deeper understanding of the data structures and the transformation process involved, please feel free to ask any questions or request assistance with MongoDB or data structure-related concerns.", 'temperature': 0.0, 'best_of': 1, 'max_tokens': 1667, 'logprobs': None, 'stream': True, 'stream_options': {'include_usage': True}}
{'model': '/data/model/deepseek-aiDeepSeek-R1-Distill-Qwen-7B', 'prompt': 'Here are the 10 dot points, including an anecdote about Sir Dixon:\n\n* The fact-finder should have access to all information that can support rational reasoning about the facts at issue in proceedings.\n* All relevant information should be considered by the court to avoid incorrect verdicts.\n* The only principle of admission in the law of evidence is that relevant evidence should be used.\n* The principle of admission is given expression in section 56(1) of the uniform evidence legislation.\n* Exclusionary rules may exclude evidence that has only marginal relevance to the inquiry.\n* The principle is not a guarantee that court decisions will be based on every piece of relevant information.\n* Justice Gageler recounts a story about Sir Owen Dixon, who said that a third of the facts are excluded due to normal frailty and memory, negligence of the profession, and archaic laws of evidence.\n* The law of evidence cannot address the loss of evidence through external exigencies or parties who decide to withhold relevant information.\n* Substantive law now bars some destruction of evidence, but preserves the parties\' role by penalizing jurors who conduct their own research into a case.\n* The use of ouija boards by jurors, which is characterized as "irresponsible," may now be criminal.', 'temperature': 0.0, 'best_of': 1, 'max_tokens': 1062, 'logprobs': None, 'stream': True, 'stream_options': {'include_usage': True}}
