{'model': '/data/model/deepseek-aiDeepSeek-R1-Distill-Qwen-7B', 'prompt': 'The code is written in PlainLang, which appears to be a custom programming language. The code contains various functions and instructions for different tasks, such as adding lines to figures, adjusting boxes, and beginning printing. Some functions also make use of external libraries, such as "user32.dll" and "gdi32.dll", which are Windows API libraries. It appears that the code is used to perform operations related to printing, such as setting up and adjusting printer settings, and creating and manipulating figures and shapes. There are also references to PDFs, such as creating pdf objects, and setting the pdf state\'s document flag, which implies that the code may also be used for creating and printing PDF documents.', 'temperature': 0.0, 'best_of': 1, 'max_tokens': 1071, 'logprobs': None, 'stream': True, 'stream_options': {'include_usage': True}}
