{'model': '/data/model/deepseek-aiDeepSeek-R1-Distill-Qwen-7B', 'prompt': 'Rewrite in plain English:\n\nThe new Israeli government is more right-wing than any before it, with an aim to reorganize the state and weaken democratic mechanisms. This includes reducing the power of the Supreme Court and fundamental rights. They also want to make the integration of the West Bank into Israel irreversible. This government is the result of a long-term shift in Israeli politics, with a growing right-wing majority and increasing political legitimacy for the radical right.\n\nKey points and quotes:\n\n1. The new government\'s anti-liberal impetus:\n\t* "The government intends to weaken democratic mechanisms, especially the system of checks and balances, the status of the Supreme Court, and that of fundamental rights."\n\t* "The integration of the West Bank into the legal territory of the state of Israel is to be made irreversible."\n2. Composition of the coalition:\n\t* "The coalition members consist of Likud (32 seats), the two parties of the Haredim, frequently described as “ultra-orthodox” – Shas (11) and United Torah Judaism (UTJ, 7) – as well as the radical party alliance Religious Zionism (14)."\n3. Causes of the political shift to the right:\n\t* Demographic development: "In Israel, the younger the citizen, the more politically right-wing they are."\n\t* Failure of the peace process: "Since the mid-2000s, there has been a steady downward trend of left-wing parties and a growing dominance of right-wing parties."\n\t* Haredim parties joining the right-wing camp.\n\t* Internal struggles for hegemony leading to radicalization: "Netanyahu responded by making a substantive shift to the right."\n\t* US support under President Trump: "The fact that the United States under President Donald Trump supported many of the right-wing positions did the rest to further strengthen the trend."\n\t* Accusation of corruption against Netanyahu: "To compensate for the loss of these votes, the prime minister mobilised forces on the extreme fringes of the right-wing political spectrum that were ready to protect him from corruption charges."\n4. Relationship between Likud and the extreme right:\n\t* "All these manoeuvres have resulted in the abolition of any meaningful divisions between Likud and the extreme right."\n\t* "Although they might not share all views, for Likud under Netanyahu today, there is no party on the right-wing of the political spectrum that would disqualify itself as a partner by taking positions that are too radical."', 'temperature': 0.0, 'best_of': 1, 'max_tokens': 1340, 'logprobs': None, 'stream': True, 'stream_options': {'include_usage': True}}
