{'model': '/data/model/deepseek-aiDeepSeek-R1-Distill-Qwen-7B', 'prompt': 'The E-2 classification is for aliens who are nationals of a country with which the United States maintains a qualifying treaty or an international agreement, or which has been deemed a qualifying country by legislation. They are coming to the United States to develop and direct the operations of an enterprise in which the alien has invested or is actively in the process of investing a substantial amount of capital. The petition must be filed with evidence of possession and control of capital, the ability to develop and direct the investment enterprise and the ability to generate income. An employee of an E-2 treaty investor who possesses the same nationality as the E-2 employer may also be classified as E-2. The employee must principally and primarily perform executive or supervisory duties or possess special qualifications that are essential to the successful or efficient operation of the enterprise.', 'temperature': 0.0, 'best_of': 1, 'max_tokens': 1752, 'logprobs': None, 'stream': True, 'stream_options': {'include_usage': True}}
{'model': '/data/model/deepseek-aiDeepSeek-R1-Distill-Qwen-7B', 'prompt': 'Form I-129, also known as the "Petition for a Nonimmigrant Worker," is a form used by U.S. employers to petition for a foreign worker to come temporarily to the United States to perform services or labor or to receive training. The form is used for a variety of nonimmigrant classifications, including H-1B, L-1, and O-1, among others. The form collects information about the petitioner, the beneficiary, and the requested nonimmigrant classification. It also includes instructions and information on filing fees, processing times, and other requirements. The form can be filed online or by mail, and it is handled by the U.S. Citizenship and Immigration Services (USCIS).', 'temperature': 0.0, 'best_of': 1, 'max_tokens': 1753, 'logprobs': None, 'stream': True, 'stream_options': {'include_usage': True}}
{'model': '/data/model/deepseek-aiDeepSeek-R1-Distill-Qwen-7B', 'prompt': 'Dr. Minkoff is a medical doctor who runs a large natural medicine clinic in Florida, and specializes in treating people with unsolved medical problems such as Lyme, cancer, autoimmune disease and central nervous system disease. He also owns a nutrition company called Body Health, which produces high-quality nutritional products. He also is an Ironman athlete and has done 43 of them. He believes that age is not a barrier to being active and engaged and that people should be smarter and more financially secure at 60 than they were at 40. He also believes that they can make a bigger impact and help more people. Dr. Minkoff also believes that blood flow restriction training or occlusion training is a great way to build muscle and strength, especially for older people or those who are intimidated by heavy weights. He also believes that hormone release is an incredible thing for people and that blood flow restriction training can be done with light weights, and will still produce a response.', 'temperature': 0.0, 'best_of': 1, 'max_tokens': 1347, 'logprobs': None, 'stream': True, 'stream_options': {'include_usage': True}}
