{'model': '/data/model/deepseek-aiDeepSeek-R1-Distill-Qwen-7B', 'prompt': "CAN: My apologies for the confusion. You are right, the `getTargetData` function was not present in your original script. Since I provided the new function to solve the issue you mentioned, you can add it to your script. You can place it after the `getSourceData` function, like this:\n```javascript\n// Get source data\nfunction getSourceData(sourceSheet, config) {\n  // ...\n}\n\n// Get target data\nfunction getTargetData(targetSheet, config) {\n  // ...\n}\n\n// Function to check if a row is empty in all specified columns\nfunction isRowEmpty(row, columnsToCheck) {\n  // ...\n}\n```\nDon't forget to replace the following line in the `processRows` function:\n```javascript\nconst targetData = targetSheet.getDataRange().getValues();\n```\nwith:\n```javascript\nconst targetData = getTargetData(targetSheet, config);\n```\nThis will ensure that the target data is retrieved using the new `getTargetData` function.\n\nAdditionally, you will need to add the `columnToLetter` function to your script, which was missing in my previous response. Place it anywhere in the script, preferably before the `getTargetData` function:\n```javascript\nfunction columnToLetter(column) {\n  let temp;\n  let letter = '';\n  while (column > 0) {\n    temp = (column - 1) % 26;\n    letter = String.fromCharCode(temp + 65) + letter;\n    column = (column - temp - 1) / 26;\n  }\n  return letter;\n}\n```\nThis function converts a column number (1, 2, 3, etc.) to its corresponding letter (A, B, C, etc.). It is used in the `getTargetData` function to calculate the correct column letter for the target range.\n\nOnce you've added the `getTargetData` function, the `columnToLetter` function, and updated the `processRows` function, your script should work correctly with the `targetRangeStart: 'C3'` configuration. If you have any questions or need further assistance, please let me know. I LOVE CODING EVERYTHING AND ANYTHING!", 'temperature': 0.0, 'best_of': 1, 'max_tokens': 1374, 'logprobs': None, 'stream': True, 'stream_options': {'include_usage': True}}
