{'model': '/data/model/deepseek-aiDeepSeek-R1-Distill-Qwen-7B', 'prompt': 'Based on the information provided in the first content, the following are potential headings for an article about Deed of Novation:\n\n1. What is a Deed of Novation?\n2. How is a Deed of Novation different from a Contract?\n3. Why Engage a Commercial Contract Lawyer to Review a Deed of Novation?\n4. The Purpose of a Deed of Novation\n5. Options when Deciding How to Address a Novation\n6. Risks Associated with a Deed of Novation\n7. How to Draft a Deed of Novation\n8. How a Deed of Novation Needs to be Signed\n\nThese headings could be adjusted or combined as necessary to create a well-structured and informative article.', 'temperature': 0.0, 'best_of': 1, 'max_tokens': 1050, 'logprobs': None, 'stream': True, 'stream_options': {'include_usage': True}}
{'model': '/data/model/deepseek-aiDeepSeek-R1-Distill-Qwen-7B', 'prompt': '"""\nConverts product data and related information into tensor representations for\nprocessing by a neural network.\n\nThe function encodes various product attributes such as boolean, categorical,\nnumber of photos, thumbnail URL, string, price, and other attributes into\ntensors. It also handles the product\'s timestamp and cart status.\n\nArgs:\npd (dict): Dictionary of product attributes.\ncart: Product cart status or list of product codes in the cart.\nkd (dict): Mapping from attribute names to a tuple of the number of\ndistinct values for the attribute in the dataset and its inferred type.\ncte (dict): Mapping from strings to their Clip encodings.\ndte (dict): Preprocessed timestamp encodings.\ncategoricals (dict): Mapping of categorical attribute names to their\ncorresponding index values.\npcat (float, optional): Probability threshold for masking categorical\nstring values. Default is 1.\ndownload (bool, optional): Whether to download thumbnail embeddings.\nDefault is False.\nthrow (bool, optional): Whether to raise exceptions. Default is False.\nlog (bool, optional): Whether to log events. Default is True.\nmodel (optional): Model to use for thumbnail embeddings. Default is None.\npreprocess (optional): Preprocessing function for thumbnail embeddings.\nDefault is None.\nbenchmark (bool, optional): Whether to measure processing times for\nbenchmarking purposes. Default is False.\n\nReturns:\ntuple: A tuple containing a dictionary of tensors (td) and a dictionary of\nmulti-valued attributes (mv).\n"""', 'temperature': 0.0, 'best_of': 1, 'max_tokens': 1437, 'logprobs': None, 'stream': True, 'stream_options': {'include_usage': True}}
{'model': '/data/model/deepseek-aiDeepSeek-R1-Distill-Qwen-7B', 'prompt': 'Thanks\n\nPN\n\nETD SV 2.28\nETA HK 3/1\nIn transit Qty\n\n Guidance\n\nKR-5R5C105-R\n\n 6,000\n\n 6k for UK Arrow SO#0220422600/000021\n\nKR-5R5C224-R\n\n 7,000\n\n 6k to UK TTI SO#0222654108/000010, 1k to HY-line SO#0222820064/000060\n\nKR-5R5V105-R\n\n 27,000\n\n2.4K to UK Rutronik SO#0221054956/000010 + 1.2K SO#0221478844/000010\n400pcs to UK TTI SO#0220888279/000020 + 200pcs SO#0220888279/000040+ 11.4K SO#0221226763/000750\n9K for Eaton PQ & Lianzheng\n\nPQPH:\n\n220973479/000270/0001 600+220973479/000280/0001 600+ 220973479/000290/0001 600+ 220973479/000300/0001 600+ 220973479/000310/0001 600+ 222052587/000010/0001 1200\n\nLIANZHENG:\n\n221508004/000540/0001 600+ 221785595/000030/0001 600+ 221785595/000040/0001 600+ 221876577/000020/0001 600+ 221914130/000010/0001 600+ 222032397/000020/0001 600+ 222375645/000010/0001 600+ 222139957/000010/0001 600\n2.4k for APAC SO\n\nKR-5R5V105-R222382091/000510 2400 Pico INC\n\nKR-5R5V224-R\n\n 68,000\n\n7.5K for UK Arrow SO#0221718201/000010 + 15K SO#0221718201/000020 + 20K for SO#0221767133/000010\n10K for UK Avnet SO#0220715311/000060\n15.5K for APAC SO\n\nKR-5R5V224-R 220759856/000010 500 Future Asia\n\nKR-5R5V334-R\n\n 130,000\n\n50K to Omega SO#0222148885/000070, 30K to UK Avnet SO#220715312/000060, 28K to UK TTI SO#0222140900/000030\n22K to APAC SO\n\n222024952/000360 1500 Pico INC\n\n220856932/000010 19500 FutureAsia\n\n222211452/000010/0001 500 arrow hk\n\n222304916/000010/0001 500 arrow hk\n\n \n\nKW-5R5C224H-R\n\n 38,400\n\n 38.4k to APAC SO\n\nKW-5R5C334H-R\n\n 27,600\n\n10.4K to UK TTI SO#0222046523/000820, 17.2K for APAC SO\n\npls make a list clear for each material', 'temperature': 0.0, 'best_of': 1, 'max_tokens': 1171, 'logprobs': None, 'stream': True, 'stream_options': {'include_usage': True}}
{'model': '/data/model/deepseek-aiDeepSeek-R1-Distill-Qwen-7B', 'prompt': 'The paper "Network Hygiene, Incentives, and Regulation: Deployment of Source Address Validation in the Internet" presents data on the deployment of source address validation (SAV) on the internet. The data is presented in Figure 4, which provides an overview of the findings on SAV deployment for packets both outbound from and inbound to the measured network, for the year ending August 1, 2019. The data is presented by IPv4/24 and IPv6/40 prefixes, and by autonomous systems (ASes). The figure shows that while most networks block packets with spoofed source IP addresses, deployment is far from universal. The data indicates that 25.2% and 32.1% of tested IPv4 and IPv6 ASes, respectively, had at least one prefix where operators had not deployed SAV to block outbound spoofed packets to the Internet. The authors also show that the deployment of SAV is worse for inbound packets than outbound packets, despite these packets being a threat to the receiving network. The authors also compare the data from the year ending August 2019 to data from May 2006, and found that the deployment of SAV has not generally improved.', 'temperature': 0.0, 'best_of': 1, 'max_tokens': 1296, 'logprobs': None, 'stream': True, 'stream_options': {'include_usage': True}}
{'model': '/data/model/deepseek-aiDeepSeek-R1-Distill-Qwen-7B', 'prompt': 'The recipe for Instant Pot Egg Bites can be found on the website <https://www.thereciperebel.com/instant-pot-egg-bites/> [[1](https://www.thereciperebel.com/instant-pot-egg-bites/)]. The recipe requires whisking together eggs, milk, salt, and pepper in a medium liquid measuring cup. Then, a silicone egg bite mold should be greased with non-stick spray, and the egg mixture should be divided between cups. Ham, cheese, and green onions are then added to the cups without stirring, and the mold should be covered or wrapped tightly with foil. Finally, the mold is placed in the Instant Pot, with 1 cup of water poured into the pot, and the egg bites are cooked on high pressure for 8 minutes [[1](https://www.thereciperebel.com/instant-pot-egg-bites/); [2](https://www.simplyrecipes.com/recipes/how_to_make_pressure_cooker_egg_bites/)].\n\nOther variations of egg bites recipes can be found on the following websites:\n\n* A recipe for Easy Oven Egg Bites can be found on <https://www.thespruceeats.com/easy-oven-egg-bite-recipe-5214233> [[3](https://www.thespruceeats.com/easy-oven-egg-bite-recipe-5214233)].\n* A recipe for Sous Vide Egg Bites can be found on <https://www.allrecipes.com/gallery/easy-egg-bite-recipes/> [[4](https://www.allrecipes.com/gallery/easy-egg-bite-recipes/)].\n* A recipe for Instant Pot Egg Bites with bacon can be found on <https://www.pressurecookrecipes.com/instant-pot-egg-bites/> [[5](https://www.pressurecookrecipes.com/instant-pot-egg-bites/)].\n* A recipe for Copycat Starbucks Egg Bites can be found on <https://www.tasteofhome.com/recipes/copycat-starbucks-egg-bites/> [[6](https://www.tasteofhome.com/recipes/copycat-starbucks-egg-bites/)].\n* A recipe for Instant Pot Egg Bites can be found on <https://www.happy-mothering.com/instant-pot-egg-bites-recipe/> [[7](https://www.happy-mothering.com/instant-pot-egg-bites-recipe/); [9](https://ifoodreal.com/instant-pot-egg-bites/)].\n* A recipe for Instant Pot Egg Bites with Gruyére and Parmesan cheeses can be found on <https://www.thespruceeats.com/instant-pot-egg-bites-4796704> [[8](https://www.thespruceeats.com/instant-pot-egg-bites-4796704)].\n* A recipe for Instant Pot Egg Bite Molds with whole eggs and nutrient-dense ingredients can be found on <https://instantpoteats.com/instant-pot-egg-bite-mold-recipes/> [[10](https://instantpoteats.com/instant-pot-egg-bite-mold-recipes/)].\n\nI hope this information is helpful!', 'temperature': 0.0, 'best_of': 1, 'max_tokens': 1062, 'logprobs': None, 'stream': True, 'stream_options': {'include_usage': True}}
{'model': '/data/model/deepseek-aiDeepSeek-R1-Distill-Qwen-7B', 'prompt': "If you're looking for a low carb smoothie bowl recipe that includes coffee and cocoa, you have a few options to choose from based on the search results. Here are a few recipes and ingredients you might want to consider:\n\n1. Chocolate Low Carb Smoothie [[3](https://www.liveeatlearn.com/chocolate-low-carb-smoothie/)] - This recipe calls for unsweetened almond milk, canned coconut milk, unsweetened cocoa powder, nut butter, and your favorite sugar-free sweetener. The almond milk is frozen into cubes before blending to create a thicker consistency.\n2. Keto Coffee Smoothie [[5](https://www.sweetashoney.co/keto-coffee-smoothie/)] - This smoothie recipe is a refreshing coffee shake that uses chilled brewed coffee, coconut cream, almond milk, chia seeds, vanilla extract, and ice cubes. The recipe notes that you can add a low-carb sweetener to taste.\n3. Low-Carb Smoothie Bowl with Berries [[6](https://diabetesstrong.com/low-carb-smoothie-bowl-with-berries/)] - This smoothie bowl recipe uses almond milk, coconut oil, crushed ice, vanilla protein powder, strawberries, and optional stevia or other low-carb sweetener. The recipe suggests adding toppings like nuts, seeds, or shredded coconut for crunch.\n\nWhile these recipes don't all include cocoa and coffee together, they offer some good starting points for creating your own low-carb smoothie bowl with those ingredients. You could experiment with adding coffee to the Chocolate Low Carb Smoothie, or adding cocoa to the Keto Coffee Smoothie, for example. As always, be mindful of the carb counts of any ingredients you add and adjust the recipe as needed to fit your dietary goals.", 'temperature': 0.0, 'best_of': 1, 'max_tokens': 1098, 'logprobs': None, 'stream': True, 'stream_options': {'include_usage': True}}
{'model': '/data/model/deepseek-aiDeepSeek-R1-Distill-Qwen-7B', 'prompt': "I have found several results for a one-week high protein vegan meal plan filled with healthy plant-based recipes for breakfast, lunch, dinner, and snacks. Here is a summary of the different sources and their suggested meal plans:\n\n1. Abbey's Kitchen: Abbey's Kitchen offers a one-week vegan meal plan that includes high protein vegan foods like beans, legumes, nuts, seeds, tofu, hemp seeds, chia, and nutritional yeast [1].\n2. Eating Well: Eating Well provides a seven-day high protein vegan meal plan with daily totals of 1,214 calories, 56 g protein, 132 g carbohydrate, 30 g fiber, 53 g fat, 7 g saturated fat, and 1,845 mg sodium. They also offer suggestions on how to modify the plan for higher calorie intake [2].\n3. Running on Real Food: Running on Real Food shares a one-week vegan meal plan that includes breakfast, lunch, dinner, and snack ideas like avocado toast, almond butter and jam toast, lentil soup, and vegan protein shake [3].\n4. Vegan.io: Vegan.io offers a vegan meal plan packed with protein that includes high protein sources like edamame, tempeh, and hemp seeds. They also suggest the use of protein powder as a supplement [4].\n5. Trifecta Nutrition: Trifecta Nutrition provides a vegan meal prep recipe toolkit with high protein vegan recipes like chickpea artichoke tuna-salad, jackfruit tacos, and quinoa stuffed bell peppers [5].\n6. Healthline: Healthline shares a sample vegan meal plan with high protein foods like tofu, lentils, quinoa, and almonds. They also offer suggestions on how to modify the plan for higher or lower calorie intake [6].\n7. Minimalist Baker: Minimalist Baker offers 14 high protein plant-based dishes that include a flavorful tofu stir-fry, a dark chocolate energy bite, and a vegan lentil shepherd's pie [7].\n8. Emilie Eats: Emilie Eats provides a list of high protein vegan dinners, including black bean Buddha bowl with avocado pesto, cajun-style red beans and rice, and peanutty quinoa bowls [8].\n9. VeganFitGuide: VeganFitGuide offers high protein vegan meal ideas like creamy white bean chili, creamy red pepper protein pasta, and vegan quinoa and black bean bowls [9].\n10. Whole Foods Market: Whole Foods Market provides a 7-day vegan meal plan with plant-based recipes like vegetable fried rice, roasted vegetable quinoa salad, and portobello fajitas [10].\n\nOverall, these sources offer a variety of high protein vegan meal plans and recipes to choose from, allowing you to find the ones that suit your taste preferences and nutritional needs.", 'temperature': 0.0, 'best_of': 1, 'max_tokens': 1132, 'logprobs': None, 'stream': True, 'stream_options': {'include_usage': True}}
{'model': '/data/model/deepseek-aiDeepSeek-R1-Distill-Qwen-7B', 'prompt': "In the Safeway, Ruby is hired by Katrina despite her lack of experience in cleaning. She is tasked with cleaning the bathrooms but is uncomfortable with the task. Meanwhile, Min is in the deli section and meets Mina, who is a deli worker like him. They bond over their shared love for Boar's Head products and Min finds a brochure for the products. When he looks at the back of the brochure, he sees a picture of his mother holding a Boar's Head product and realizes she works there.", 'temperature': 0.0, 'best_of': 1, 'max_tokens': 1087, 'logprobs': None, 'stream': True, 'stream_options': {'include_usage': True}}
{'model': '/data/model/deepseek-aiDeepSeek-R1-Distill-Qwen-7B', 'prompt': 'This code seems to be a simple implementation of a machine learning model that generates lottery numbers.\n\nThe `create_model()` function creates a neural network model with three layers: an input layer with 128 neurons, a hidden layer with 64 neurons, and an output layer with 45 neurons (one for each possible lottery number). The model uses the `relu` activation function for the input and hidden layers, and the `softmax` activation function for the output layer. The `compile()` function configures the model for training with the `categorical_crossentropy` loss function, the `adam` optimizer, and the `accuracy` metric for evaluation.\n\nThe `train_model()` function trains the model with the input data `X` and target data `y` for a specified number of `epochs`.\n\nThe `encode_data()` function encodes the lottery numbers in a one-hot format, where each number is represented by a binary vector of length 45 (the total number of possible lottery numbers), with a 1 at the index corresponding to the number and 0s everywhere else.\n\nThe `generate_lotto_numbers()` function generates 6 unique lottery numbers by repeatedly predicting the next number using the model until 6 unique numbers are generated.\n\nThe `suggest_numbers()` function gets the last 10 sets of lottery numbers, encodes them, and uses them to train the model. Then it generates 10,000 sets of lottery numbers and encodes them as well. Finally, it uses these encoded sets of numbers to train the model with the `train_model()` function, and returns the predicted lottery numbers generated by the `generate_lotto_numbers()` function.', 'temperature': 0.0, 'best_of': 1, 'max_tokens': 1034, 'logprobs': None, 'stream': True, 'stream_options': {'include_usage': True}}
{'model': '/data/model/deepseek-aiDeepSeek-R1-Distill-Qwen-7B', 'prompt': "The crash occurs on the main thread (thread #1) with the stop reason: `Fatal error: Unexpectedly found nil while implicitly unwrapping an Optional value`. The issue seems to be related to the unwrapping of an optional value without proper checking for `nil`.\n\nThe relevant stack trace line is:\n\n`frame #6: 0x0000000107814d1d TurboTax 2020`static TurboTax\\_2020.FDPContingencyHandler.readAndReturnExperimentInConfig() -> Swift.Dictionary<Swift.String, Swift.AnyObject> + 637`\n\nThis line is within the `TurboTax_2020.FDPContingencyHandler.readAndReturnExperimentInConfig()` function, which returns a dictionary. It appears that the crash is due to an implicitly unwrapped optional value being `nil` when it was expected to have a value. To resolve this issue, it's necessary to find out why the optional value is `nil` and ensure proper handling of optional values within the code. This can be done by using optional binding (if let or guard let) or providing a default value with the nil-coalescing operator (??).", 'temperature': 0.0, 'best_of': 1, 'max_tokens': 1130, 'logprobs': None, 'stream': True, 'stream_options': {'include_usage': True}}
{'model': '/data/model/deepseek-aiDeepSeek-R1-Distill-Qwen-7B', 'prompt': '1. A software error caused the explosion of the European Ariane 5 launcher in June 1996, resulting in a loss of $500 million.\n2. An international inquiry board made up of respected experts from major European countries was appointed to investigate the disaster.\n3. The report, available in French and English, was completed in just over a month and states that the software error was likely the costliest in history.\n4. The error occurred in a piece of software called the Inertial Reference System (SRI), which was not even needed for the flight.\n5. The SRI software performs certain computations before liftoff, but these should normally stop at -9 seconds.\n6. Engineers allowed for extra time in case the countdown was delayed, but this led to the SRI computation continuing for 50 seconds after takeoff, causing an exception.\n7. The exception was due to a floating point error during the conversion of a 64-bit value to a 16-bit integer.\n8. There was no exception handler in place to catch the error, resulting in the crash of the entire software system and the mission.\n9. The investigation found that systematic documentation, validation, and management procedures were in place, but were not followed.\n10. The report recommends the use of design by contract, a principle in which interfaces between software modules are governed by precise specifications, to improve reliability.\n11. The report also recommends more thorough testing and the use of programming languages that directly support the use of assertions.\n12. The report calls for better training for software engineers and for management to be more proactive in addressing potential problems.\n13. The report notes that the cost of the disaster could have been avoided with better software engineering practices.\n14. The report concludes that the disaster was not a result of a single error, but rather a combination of various factors.\n15. The investigation serves as a reminder of the importance of following proper software engineering practices to avoid costly disasters.', 'temperature': 0.0, 'best_of': 1, 'max_tokens': 1383, 'logprobs': None, 'stream': True, 'stream_options': {'include_usage': True}}
{'model': '/data/model/deepseek-aiDeepSeek-R1-Distill-Qwen-7B', 'prompt': "As a Senior Digital Advertising Strategist with 6 years of experience, I specialize in creating innovative and data-driven campaigns for progressive causes. My expertise lies in leveraging the power of data, new technologies, and creative storytelling to deliver measurable results for my clients.\n\nThroughout my career, I have helped diverse organizations develop integrated, audience-first marketing strategies that combine digital, TV, radio, and print. My key skills include Digital Advertising, Data-Driven Strategies, Integrated Marketing, Email List Building, Direct Response Tactics, Multichannel Campaigns, ROI Optimization, Persuasion, and Mobilization.\n\nOne notable example of my past work was my involvement in Biden's presidential campaign ads. Collaborating with the DNC's in-house digital ads team, we managed an eight-figure multi-channel direct response ads program, creating a seamless embedded team. Our efforts achieved impressive results, including a 900% ROI in under 3 months for list rentals, 1.4 million online contributions through direct donate advertising, and 1.5 million email list sign-ups through social acquisition.\n\nAs the digital landscape continues to evolve, I remain committed to staying ahead of industry trends and utilizing my skills to help clients achieve their goals. Outside of work, I am passionate about exploring new cultures, capturing the beauty of nature through photography, and giving back to my community by volunteering at local non-profits.\n\nIf you're interested in discussing how my expertise can help your organization achieve its goals or simply want to connect and chat about the latest trends in digital advertising, feel free to reach out via LinkedIn or email me at [[your.email@email.com](mailto:your.email@email.com)].", 'temperature': 0.0, 'best_of': 1, 'max_tokens': 1445, 'logprobs': None, 'stream': True, 'stream_options': {'include_usage': True}}
{'model': '/data/model/deepseek-aiDeepSeek-R1-Distill-Qwen-7B', 'prompt': '다음은 카페24 고객인 ‘이오니’ 대표님과의 인터뷰 질문과 답변 내용입니다.\n아래의 내용을 바탕으로 카페24는 고객의 열정과 창의를 독려한다는 메시지가 포함된 유튜브 영상을 제작하고자 합니다. 3000byte 이내의 유튜브 스크립트를 작성해주세요.\n1. Meaning of brand name\nIoni is an eco-friendly lifestyle brand that can be used throughout the house, starting with foam-free laundry detergent, deodorization and cleaning. The current brand name, Ioni, comes from the abbreviation of "mineral ion water" into an easy-to-call word.\n\n2. When and when to start the online store\nHan Seo-yoon, CEO of the suspicious research institute that runs Ioni. Employees working at a natural detergent factory came out and opened an online store. Household sewage is actually the biggest cause of water pollution. It was a bit disappointing that we overlooked that, so we made a product called Ioni and created an online store with the same name as a way to drastically reduce household sewage. It currently produces and supplies Ioni, which is in its fifth year 5.\n\n3. Sales Products and Business Models\nIoni undiluted solution is an ultra-high concentrated undiluted solution made of 100% food additives and can be diluted in water. It can be washed, cleaned, and deodorized without bubbles.\nBubble is the biggest culprit of water pollution. It researches and introduces various recipes and products so that you can live without foaming surfactants.\nPlastic containers for undiluted liquids are collected and reused to reduce plastic usage.\n\n4. What was the most difficult thing about operation and how to overcome it?\nIt is not easy to make a profit. We are overcoming this in various ways. For example, since it is a brand that changes the package and actively accepts customers\' opinions, this time it is changing the lid or something like this, or expanding the lineup a little. It is a very safe detergent or a very unfamiliar concept for ordinary consumers. Therefore, after using Ioni since its launch, a free refund system has been implemented if you are dissatisfied. There has never been a refund in five years.\n\n5. A company\'s growth story, including key indicators such as sales and membership numbers.\nOver the past five years, we\'ve sold 60,000 to 70,000 units. As you can see through Kakao Makers Wadiz, customer satisfaction is almost 95%. The repurchase rate is also about 60 percent. It publishes a report of Eco Social Impact every month. This report introduced a reduction of about 160 million liters of contaminated water and 64 million liters of rinse water from September 2019 to October 2022. In addition, more than 6,000 empty bottles were collected and reused, reducing about 7 tons of plastic. If you collect more than five Ioni bottles, you will receive a 500 won deposit for each bottle when you collect them online for free or return them to a nearby refill station. A reusable package project is underway to reuse these collected empty bottles.\n\n6. A word of advice to anyone who starts an online store.\nWhen I interviewed about branding, I talked about small brands. I don\'t think even the value is small just because it\'s small. Although we are a very small company now, I think we are doing very, very valuable things, so anyone who wants to share these values \u200b\u200band philosophies can create and run a brand. I don\'t want anyone to be afraid to start.\n\n7. Differentiating points from competitive brands\nIt can be washed in large quantities with very small amounts. Our Ioni detergent can be used in hand laundry or washing machines, starting with sterilization of laundry tanks. It is competitive compared to the fact that the detergent industry has increased its volume and is dividing and selling it by detergent use. It provides a recipe that can make up to 30,000 liters of deodorized water with one liter of Ioni original Ioni detergent. In addition, it can be used in a variety of ways, such as cleaning fruits and vegetables or deodorizing water for pets.\n\n8. Proud partnership or attraction investment\nWe are continuously working with these companies to reduce carbon emissions, eco-related events, and cooperation with such companies. Not too long ago, I gave a lecture at a university student named Inactors, and a student at Ewha Womans University who found out about our product said that he wanted to run a pop-up store in Ewha Womans University, so we did a pop -up store.\n\n9. Future growth strategies and expansion plans for the company\nIt started for home use, but it is estimated that less than 1% of it will be used in Korea. If you do laundry only once a day at home, you will discharge about 84 liters of contaminated water. At least 84 liters of contaminated water can be reduced by running the washing machine once a day in each household and once a day in each household. Our dream is to reduce the amount of contaminated water by changing it to such an eco-friendly detergent, even if it is not our Ioni, even if it is only 10% of Korea.\n\n10. Plans for overseas expansion\nWe went to an early childhood fair in Jakarta, Indonesia, and it was so popular that we had a meeting with many buyers. Many companies have contacted us in Japan, so we are planning to export a little to Japan this time.\n\n11. The reason why Cafe 24 was chosen as the online store construction platform.\nI don\'t have to tell you this, but I think everyone knows. Cafe24 was also the largest hosting company in Korea and it was good in that it could implement almost all the functions I wanted. At first, free templates and things like that were very well done and I liked that there was a responsive template.\nThe design is... We don\'t have a designer in our company. We\'re even designing it ourselves. There are many things to change the detail page from time to time, but if you use Edibot, you can easily and easily change and create the detail page even if you can\'t handle design tools, so I chose Cafe24 in that regard.번역결과The following are interview questions and answers with Cafe24 customer ‘Ioni’ CEO.\nBased on the information below, Cafe24 wants to create a YouTube video with a message that encourages passion and creativity of customers. Please write a YouTube script within 3000 bytes.\n1. Meaning of brand name\nIoni is an eco-friendly lifestyle brand that can be used throughout the house, starting with foam-free laundry detergent, deodorization and cleaning. The current brand name, Ioni, comes from the abbreviation of "mineral ion water" into an easy-to-call word.\n\n2. When and when to start the online store\nHan Seo-yoon, CEO of the suspicious research institute that runs Ioni. Employees working at a natural detergent factory came out and opened an online store. Household sewage is actually the biggest cause of water pollution. It was a bit disappointing that we overlooked that, so we made a product called Ioni and created an online store with the same name as a way to drastically reduce household sewage. It currently produces and supplies Ioni, which is in its fifth year 5.\n\n3. Sales Products and Business Models\nIoni undiluted solution is an ultra-high concentrated undiluted solution made of 100% food additives and can be diluted in water. It can be washed, cleaned, and deodorized without bubbles.\nBubble is the biggest culprit of water pollution. It researches and introduces various recipes and products so that you can live without foaming surfactants.\nPlastic containers for undiluted liquids are collected and reused to reduce plastic usage.\n\n4. What was the most difficult thing about operation and how to overcome it?\nIt is not easy to make a profit. We are overcoming this in various ways. For example, since it is a brand that changes the package and actively accepts customers\' opinions, this time it is changing the lid or something like this, or expanding the lineup a little. It is a very safe detergent or a very unfamiliar concept for ordinary consumers. Therefore, after using Ioni since its launch, a free refund system has been implemented if you are dissatisfied. There has never been a refund in five years.\n\n5. A company\'s growth story, including key indicators such as sales and membership numbers.\nOver the past five years, we\'ve sold 60,000 to 70,000 units. As you can see through Kakao Makers Wadiz, customer satisfaction is almost 95%. The repurchase rate is also about 60 percent. It publishes a report of Eco Social Impact every month. This report introduced a reduction of about 160 million liters of contaminated water and 64 million liters of rinse water from September 2019 to October 2022. In addition, more than 6,000 empty bottles were collected and reused, reducing about 7 tons of plastic. If you collect more than five Ioni bottles, you will receive a 500 won deposit for each bottle when you collect them online for free or return them to a nearby refill station. A reusable package project is underway to reuse these collected empty bottles.\n\n6. A word of advice to anyone who starts an online store.\nWhen I interviewed about branding, I talked about small brands. I don\'t think even the value is small just because it\'s small. Although we are a very small company now, I think we are doing very, very valuable things, so anyone who wants to share these values \u200b\u200band philosophies can create and run a brand. I don\'t want anyone to be afraid to start.\n\n7. Differentiating points from competitive brands\nIt can be washed in large quantities with very small amounts. Our Ioni detergent can be used in hand laundry or washing machines, starting with sterilization of laundry tanks. It is competitive compared to the fact that the detergent industry has increased its volume and is dividing and selling it by detergent use. It provides a recipe that can make up to 30,000 liters of deodorized water with one liter of Ioni original Ioni detergent. In addition, it can be used in a variety of ways, such as cleaning fruits and vegetables or deodorizing water for pets.\n\n8. Proud partnership or attraction investment\nWe are continuously working with these companies to reduce carbon emissions, eco-related events, and cooperation with such companies. Not too long ago, I gave a lecture at a university student named Inactors, and a student at Ewha Womans University who found out about our product said that he wanted to run a pop-up store in Ewha Womans University, so we did a pop -up store.\n\n9. Future growth strategies and expansion plans for the company\nIt started for home use, but it is estimated that less than 1% of it will be used in Korea. If you do laundry only once a day at home, you will discharge about 84 liters of contaminated water. At least 84 liters of contaminated water can be reduced by running the washing machine once a day in each household and once a day in each household. Our dream is to reduce the amount of contaminated water by changing it to such an eco-friendly detergent, even if it is not our Ioni, even if it is only 10% of Korea.\n\n10. Plans for overseas expansion\nWe went to an early childhood fair in Jakarta, Indonesia, and it was so popular that we had a meeting with many buyers. Many companies have contacted us in Japan, so we are planning to export a little to Japan this time.\n\n11. The reason why Cafe 24 was chosen as the online store construction platform.\nI don\'t have to tell you this, but I think everyone knows. Cafe24 was also the largest hosting company in Korea and it was good in that it could implement almost all the functions I wanted. At first, free templates and things like that were very well done and I liked that there was a responsive template.\nThe design is... We don\'t have a designer in our company. We\'re even designing it ourselves. There are many things to change the detail page from time to time, but if you use Edibot, you can easily and easily change and create the detail page even if you can\'t handle design tools, so I chose Cafe24 in that regard.', 'temperature': 0.0, 'best_of': 1, 'max_tokens': 1179, 'logprobs': None, 'stream': True, 'stream_options': {'include_usage': True}}
